{
	"_comment": "THIRD-PERSON in-hand GPS - what OTHER players (and your own 3rd-person camera) see. SEPARATE from GpsDevice_held_v1.rend on purpose: a .rend has no transform field, so the pose lives baked in the mesh, and the FP pose Eric accepted on build 33 must not move. Generated by tools/make_held_dae.py --scale 2.7 --tx -0.393 --ty 0.078 --tz -0.014 --out gps_device_held_tp_v5.dae --matsfx _tp5. The offset slides the joint OFF the screen and onto the orange body (Eric, 8/11: thumb on the orange, not the screen) - measured, not eyeballed: the screen spans -0.705..-0.110 and the joint sits at 0, clearing it by 0.110 with 0.216 of body still outboard - build 38 used 0.210/0.116 and Eric read that as the hand hanging off the edge. Paths MUST stay expanded $CONTENT_<localId>. Bump the _v suffix whenever the mesh changes: the engine caches meshes by path.",
